# ACS Prototype Development Rules

## Project Context
This is a prototyping workspace for Red Hat Advanced Cluster Security (RHACS/ACS) UI designs.
- Prototypes are built with React + PatternFly 6
- Reference code from StackRox is in `stackrox-upstream/` (read-only)
- Figma designs are the source of truth for UI

## Figma to Code Process
When given a Figma URL:
1. Use `get_design_context` MCP tool to analyze the design
2. Identify all PatternFly components needed
3. Check `stackrox-upstream/ui/apps/platform/src/` for existing patterns
4. Create prototype in `src/pages/`

## Component Guidelines
- Use PatternFly 6 components from `@patternfly/react-core`
- Use `@patternfly/react-table` for tables
- Use `@patternfly/react-icons` for icons
- Match StackRox styling with CSS from `src/styles/`

## File Organization
- Pages go in `src/pages/`
- Reusable components go in `src/components/`
- Assets (SVGs, images) go in `src/assets/`
- CSS files go in `src/styles/`

## Key StackRox Reference Locations
- Header/Masthead: `stackrox-upstream/ui/apps/platform/src/Containers/MainPage/Header/`
- Navigation: `stackrox-upstream/ui/apps/platform/src/Containers/MainPage/Navigation/`
- Vulnerabilities: `stackrox-upstream/ui/apps/platform/src/Containers/Vulnerabilities/`
- Branding/Logo: `stackrox-upstream/ui/apps/platform/src/constants/productBranding.ts`

## Branding
- Always use the official RHACS logo from `src/assets/RHACS-Logo.svg`
- Use PatternFly color tokens, not hardcoded colors
- Page title should be "Red Hat Advanced Cluster Security"

## Interactive States
When implementing interactive prototypes:
1. Identify all states from Figma frames
2. Use React `useState` for state management
3. Implement dropdowns with PatternFly Select/MenuToggle
4. Use PatternFly Modal for dialogs

## Safety
- `stackrox-upstream/` is READ-ONLY reference material
- Never modify files in `stackrox-upstream/`
- All prototype code belongs in `src/`
